{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1759229620527549]*{color}:
Hi! The AZ reporting was implemented before the team split and is technically owned by the Expansion team, though one of the assumptions at the time of the team split was that it might be _eventually_ handed over when there is not more active development needed there. I have no clue how EMs and product would want to handle this request right now, but Expansion team is still handling technical improvements and fixes for this integration.

Regardless of which team is responsible for it, the complexity comes from how the filtering is technically defined. If it is for specific category IDs, then this is simple (can consider ), but there is configuration overhead each time new taxi categories are added. If it has to be more generic based on category groups, then there would be less configuration overhead, but implementation will need a bit more effort since order does not list category groups (group can be obtained using SearchCategoryIMD, perhaps there is a lighter alternative as well).

Another important area to consider is that in both of those options the same driver in principle can take both taxi and non-taxi orders if they see both taxi and non-taxi categories, which means that the total reported might not match the total actual payout to the driver. The AZ integration, I think, does not report total payouts, but you probably want to double-check as Commerce might be reporting summary data for tax purposes separately from this integration.
{quote}

