Investigating the issue i’ve found a couple of other bugs related to the container name size:

# If an SDG has a service with a service name > 63 characters (actually, it could be even less, depending on the amount of containers in the SDG), this SDG will fail to start (container name will be more than 63 characters as we add container index to the end of the container name (e.g. {{${container_name}-${index}}})
# If a service has more than 1 container instance (it could be an SDG or an average deployment) and its name is > 63 characters, the deployment will fail (same reason - we add index to the end of the container name)
# HPA fails in case the service name is > 63 characters as we use ContainerResource in HPA to monitor resources. ContainerService is set per container by container name. We create container name based on the service name and pass it to the ServiceResouce non-truncated. In this case, the deployment will actually succeed but it would fail to create an HPA.

